# LUXE — Shopping Platform Backend (Go)
# Cursor / AI rules — follow for every new task
# See also: AGENTS.md, documentation/architecture.md, .cursor/skills/ (/new-api-entity, /add-api-endpoint)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# 1. PROJECT OVERVIEW
description: |
  Production-grade Go e-commerce API (Gin, GORM, PostgreSQL, JWT).
  Layered flow:

    HTTP Request → Handler → Service facade → Application → Domain → Postgres (GORM)

  Optional packages sit beside this core:
    - internal/infrastructure/integrations/  (Stripe, R2 — external APIs)
    - internal/infrastructure/asynq/         (Asynq job queue abstraction)
    - internal/shared/observability/         (Sentry, OpenTelemetry)
    - internal/interfaces/http/middleware/   (auth, CORS, logging, tracing)
    - internal/shared/health/                  (liveness / readiness)

  All JSON API responses use utils.Response helpers (success, data, message, code).
  Statuses, roles, routes constants live in internal/constants.

  Wire dependencies in internal/application/bootstrap/wire.go (bootstrap.NewServices) and
  internal/interfaces/http/handlers/container.go (NewContainer).

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 2. ARCHITECTURE — DATA ACCESS (IMPORTANT)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
architecture:
  default_pattern: |
    Handlers call thin service facades in internal/services/.
    Facades delegate to internal/application/<ctx>/ (commands/queries).
    Application uses domain ports; GORM lives in internal/infrastructure/postgres/.

  repositories: |
    GORM implementations in internal/infrastructure/postgres/*_repository.go.
    Application layers depend on repository interfaces, not *gorm.DB (checkout is the
    intentional exception for multi-service transactions).

  service_responsibilities:
    - Thin facade: implement handler-facing interfaces, delegate to application layer
    - Cross-cutting: workflow sync, WebSocket, job handler registration (registry.go)
    - Checkout: transaction orchestration across payment/coupon/inventory (legacy *gorm.DB)

  handler_responsibilities:
    - Bind request → DTO, validate with validator
    - Pass c.Request.Context() to services
    - Map errors to utils.Response — NO business logic, NO direct DB access

  forbidden:
    - Business logic in handlers
    - Direct gorm.DB in handlers
    - Fake / dev-only shortcuts in production code paths
    - Demo product data in new Goose migrations

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 3. CLEAN CODE PRINCIPLES (always)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
clean_code:
  - Minimize scope — smallest correct diff; no unrelated refactors.
  - Match existing naming, imports, and patterns in the file you edit.
  - Reuse helpers in internal/shared/utils/ and internal/services/helpers.go.
  - Keep functions small; one responsibility per function.
  - Meaningful names — avoid data, temp, val, x.
  - Comments only for non-obvious business logic (Go: exported symbols only).
  - Pass context.Context as first parameter on new service methods; use db.WithContext(ctx).
  - Return typed domain errors from services; controllers map them to HTTP responses.
  - Use constants package for statuses — never magic strings in business logic.
  - Dependency injection via constructors — no global state.

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 4. DIRECTORY STRUCTURE
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
directories:
  cmd/api/                    # main entry, Swagger metadata comments
  internal/
    config/                   # env / Viper — not constants
    constants/                # roles, statuses, route paths
    models/                   # GORM entities ({entity}_model.go)
    application/              # use cases (commands/queries per bounded context)
    application/bootstrap/    # wire.go — composition root (NewServices)
    domain/                   # entities, ports, domain rules
    infrastructure/postgres/  # GORM repository implementations
    infrastructure/asynq/     # JobQueue (Asynq or in-memory)
    infrastructure/integrations/  # Stripe, R2, AI, PDF
    interfaces/http/
      dto/                    # request/response ({entity}_dto.go)
      handlers/               # Gin HTTP handlers, container.go
      routes/                 # route groups, middleware setup
      middleware/
    services/                 # thin facades ({entity}_service.go, registry.go)
    database/                 # connection, pool
    migrations/               # Goose SQL (internal/migrations/)
    shared/utils/             # response, errors, logger, password, email
    shared/observability/     # Sentry, OTEL tracing
    shared/health/
    jobs/                     # cron
    websocket/
  tests/
    integration/              # real Postgres; setup_test.go TestMain
    e2e/
  docs/                       # GENERATED by swag — gitignored, do not edit

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 5. NAMING CONVENTIONS
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
naming:
  files:
    models:     "{entity}_model.go"
    dto:        "{entity}_dto.go"
    services:   "{entity}_service.go"
    controllers: "{entity}_handler.go"   # under interfaces/http/handlers/
    routes:     "{entity}_routes.go"
    migrations: "{timestamp}_{name}.sql"
  code:
    structs:    PascalCase
    variables:  camelCase
    interfaces: {Entity}ServiceInterface or {Entity}Service
  database:
    tables:     snake_case plural
    columns:    snake_case
    indexes:    idx_{table}_{column}

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 6. NEW ENTITY WORKFLOW (order enforced)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
new_entity_order:
  1. make migrate-create name=create_{entity}_table   # schema only
  2. internal/models/{entity}_model.go
  3. internal/interfaces/http/dto/{entity}_dto.go
  4. internal/infrastructure/postgres/{entity}_repository.go
  5. internal/application/{entity}/ (commands, queries)
  6. internal/services/{entity}_service.go (+ register in bootstrap/wire.go)
  7. internal/interfaces/http/handlers/{entity}_handler.go (+ container.go)
  8. internal/interfaces/http/routes/{entity}_routes.go (+ routes setup)
  9. Swagger comments on handler methods
  10. make swagger
  11. tests — application/service unit tests and/or tests/integration/

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 7. GOOSE MIGRATIONS
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
goose:
  path: internal/migrations/
  create: "make migrate-create name=<name>"
  apply:  "make migrate-up"
  rollback: "make migrate-down"
  rules:
    - Always provide UP and DOWN.
    - Schema only: CREATE/ALTER TABLE, indexes, constraints.
    - Use IF NOT EXISTS / IF EXISTS for idempotency.
    - timestamptz for PostgreSQL time columns.
    - deleted_at for soft deletes when needed.
    - NO demo products, PDP filler, or dev seed data in new migrations.
    - Legacy seed migrations exist — do not copy that pattern.
    - Dev/demo seeds → scripts/ or cmd/seed (future), run only locally/staging.

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 8. MODELS (GORM)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
model_rules:
  - Package models; singular PascalCase struct names.
  - gorm tags: column, type, index, default, not null.
  - json tags for API; json:"-" for secrets (password_hash).
  - Relationships: gorm:"foreignKey:UserID;references:ID"
  - Nullable unique fields use *string or omit empty — not '' for unique indexes.

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 9. DTOs
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
dto_rules:
  - {Action}{Entity}Request / {Entity}Response
  - validate tags: required, email, omitempty, gt=0, max=100
  - Pagination: limit, offset, total, data array in list responses.
  - Timestamps as RFC3339 strings in responses when exposed.

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 10. SERVICES
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
service_rules:
  - Interface + private struct implementation.
  - Constructor: New{Entity}Service(deps...) returns interface.
  - Accept *gorm.DB and/or other services — wired in NewServices.
  - ctx context.Context first arg on new methods.
  - db.WithContext(ctx) for all queries.
  - db.Transaction for checkout, payment, inventory, multi-table updates.
  - Return utils.AppError helpers from business layer where applicable.
  - Job enqueue via tasks.JobQueue — not ad-hoc goroutines for order/shipment work.

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 11. CONTROLLERS
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
controller_rules:
  - Use utils.OK, Created, BadRequest, NotFound, ValidationError, etc.
  - Never c.JSON with raw structs except via utils helpers.
  - validator.New() per controller or shared — Struct(&req) after ShouldBindJSON.
  - Map utils.AppError codes to correct HTTP response helpers.
  - Swagger: @Summary @Tags @Router @Success @Failure @Param @Security on handlers.

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 12. SWAGGER / OPENAPI
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
swagger:
  never_edit:
    - docs/docs.go
    - docs/swagger.json
    - docs/swagger.yaml
  edit_instead:
    - Controller swagger comments
    - cmd/api/main.go (@title, @version, @host, @BasePath, security defs)
    - DTO types referenced in {object} responses
  regenerate: "make swagger"
  note: docs/ is gitignored; required locally after clone.

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 13. TESTING
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
testing:
  unit:
    - Package services; table-driven tests.
    - sqlmock for isolated DB unit tests (see auth_service_test.go).
    - utils.InitLogger in TestMain where needed.
  integration:
    - tests/integration/ against real Postgres.
    - Skip if DATABASE_URL unavailable (setup_test.go TestMain).
    - Test helpers in *_test.go only (helpers_test.go pattern).
    - Factories with unique suffix per test (seedProduct) — real inserts, not mocks.
    - Run: DATABASE_URL=... JWT_SECRET=ci_test_secret go test ./tests/integration/...
  do_not:
    - Hand-edited dummy JSON responses instead of hitting API.
    - Shared mutable test state without unique IDs/suffixes.

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 14. BACKGROUND JOBS & CRON
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
jobs:
  - tasks.JobQueue interface (EnqueueOrderProcess, EnqueueShipmentProcess).
  - REDIS_URL set → Asynq; unset → in-memory fallback.
  - Register handlers in services.Services.JobHandlers().
  - Cron in internal/jobs/ — no worker pool for order processing.

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 15. INTEGRATIONS & OBSERVABILITY
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
integrations:
  stripe:
    - internal/integrations/stripe/gateway.go
    - Config-gated; webhook at /api/v1/webhooks/stripe
    - Payment methods: mock, stripe, wallet (constants)
  r2:
    - internal/integrations/r2/client.go
    - Presign upload flow; env vars required
  observability:
    - SENTRY_DSN → Sentry middleware
    - OTEL_ENABLED=true → OTLP tracing (middleware/tracing.go)
    - Structured JSON logging (utils/logger.go, middleware/access_log.go)
  health:
    - /health/live, /health/ready, /api/v1/health

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 16. CONFIG & ENV
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
config:
  - Load via internal/config; validate in production (APP_ENV=production).
  - Secrets in .env — never commit .env.
  - See .env.example for REDIS_URL, SENTRY_DSN, OTEL_*, R2_*, Stripe keys.

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 17. MAKEFILE COMMANDS
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
makefile_commands:
  - make dev-setup          # docker postgres+redis, migrate-up
  - make run                # start API
  - make migrate-create name=<name>
  - make migrate-up / migrate-down
  - make swagger            # regenerate docs/
  - make test               # unit tests
  - make stripe-listen      # local Stripe webhooks

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 18. AI TASK CHECKLIST (before finishing any task)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ai_checklist:
  - [ ] Followed layer boundaries (no logic in handlers)
  - [ ] Used utils.Response in handlers
  - [ ] Used constants for statuses/roles
  - [ ] context.Context passed through on new code paths
  - [ ] Migrations schema-only if DB changed
  - [ ] Did not edit generated docs/
  - [ ] Registered new services in bootstrap/wire.go and handlers/container.go
  - [ ] Minimal diff — no drive-by refactors
  - [ ] go build / relevant tests pass

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 19. NO RE-REFACTOR (architecture is settled)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
architecture_frozen:
  - The layered layout (handlers → facade → application → domain → postgres) is final.
  - Add features inside existing packages; use /new-api-entity and /add-api-endpoint skills.
  - Do NOT recreate: internal/controllers/, internal/routes/, internal/dto/, internal/utils/,
    internal/middleware/, internal/tasks/, internal/integrations/, internal/observability/.
  - Do NOT move wiring back to services.go — use application/bootstrap/wire.go.
  - Do NOT put GORM in handlers or new business logic in service facades without application layer.
  - Checkout may keep *gorm.DB for cross-aggregate transactions until explicitly migrated.
